Package: ipodr
Title: Option-Implied Distress Measures and Their Identified Sets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Johannes", "Vilsmeier", , "johannes.vilsmeier@icloud.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools to extract risk-neutral distress measures from single-name
    equity option quotes and to report what the quotes do and do not identify.
    Implements a penalised maximum-entropy version of the option-implied
    probability of default of Capuano (2008) <doi:10.2139/ssrn.1339927> and
    Vilsmeier (2016) <doi:10.21314/jcf.2015.206>, with barrier-free tail
    probabilities, barrier-selection rules, model-free bounds on option prices
    and tail probabilities following Dillschneider (2026)
    <doi:10.2139/ssrn.6976498>, implied-volatility benchmarks, an anchored
    distress probability, and evaluation helpers (event windows, cluster
    bootstrap AUC comparisons and AUC bounds consistent with option prices).
